Title: What They Called Recovery
Credit: Animated feature screenplay — individual review draft
Author: Christopher Kokkinos
Draft date: 2026-09-28
Status: Individual scene draft; whole-film pass provisionally accepted, individual author review pending

INT. WATCHED HOUSE/TEMPORARY ROOM - DAY

Jackie has found a narrow chance to use a phone. Cain's people hold current evidence of her three younger siblings and can threaten them. The audience now sees more of the room first glimpsed in SC019.

Zoe sends their deliberately wrong challenge. Jackie returns the private answer. It confirms their shared history, not the safety of the device or house. Jackie tells Zoe the first route was coerced; she did not supply the second. Zoe can be hurt by the silence and understand the force behind it.

ZOE
We'll get you out.

JACKIE (TEXT)
Not if they can move the others first.

They exchange only limited questions through Voss. Jackie reports disagreement inside the legal chain and an impending move. Mac learns a phone was used but not what passed. They have a window, not a complete plan.
